          "deepDive": "**〜に即して / 〜に即した + N** means *in line with ~, in accordance with ~, based on ~*. The action is **fitted closely to** a real situation, a concrete experience or a rule: 現状に即した対応 *a response that fits the actual situation*.\n\nTwo kanji, one reading (そく):\n- **即して** — with situations, facts, experience: 実情に即して, 現実に即して, 時代に即した, 経験に即して, 事実に即して.\n- **則して** — with laws, rules, regulations (規則 contains 則): 法律に則して, 条例に則して, 規定に則して.\nThe practice below tests exactly this: 規定に則して (the rule), not 校長に則して (a person).\n\nForms: **N にそくして** + verb (adverbial), **N にそくした + N** (adnominal). You may also see 〜に即しての + N in writing.\n\nRegister: formal — the book marks it with the formal-scene icon. Common in official documents, business writing and speeches (弊社は…まいりました).\n\nCompare:\n- **〜に沿って** (N2): *along / following (a plan, policy, wishes)*; softer and more common in speech (ご要望に沿って).\n- **〜に基づいて** (N2): *based on (data, facts, a law)* as a foundation; 即して stresses *matching* the reality closely.\n- **〜に応じて** (N2): *according to, varying with* (amount, level) — changes in response to something.\n\nPitfall: the noun must be a situation/standard, not a person. ✗社長に即して → 社長の指示に従って.\n\nJLPT tip: 現状, 実情, 実態, 時代, 規定, 法律 before the blank → に即して / に則して.",
